Description: Visible texts through gettext, clock locale from LC_TIME
 The login screen of Querencia Desktop shows ReGreet in the system
 language. Visible texts (labels, buttons, tooltips, error messages and the
 PAM prompts that greetd passes on) go through glib::dgettext with the
 domain "querencia-anmeldung"; the catalog comes from po/de.po of the
 Querencia part of this source package. Untranslated texts stay English.
 A rejected password (PAM AUTH_ERR) gets a plain message instead of
 "Login failed: Pam_authenticate: AUTH_ERR".
 .
 The clock takes its locale from LC_ALL, LC_TIME or LANG ("de_DE.UTF-8"
 -> de_DE). sys-locale ignores LC_TIME and returns "de-DE", which
 chrono::Locale does not parse, so the clock fell back to en_US.
 .
 No new crates; Cargo.lock is unchanged (glib comes with gtk4/relm4).
